OL,3,GNEWSARugby honours 'Mr Music' with
OL,4,Aplaque by park bandstand
OL,5,
OL,6,FA plaque dedicated to Rugby musician
OL,7,FTom Ward, known in his hometown as "Mr
OL,8,FMusic", is to be unveiled in a
OL,9,FWarwickshire park.
OL,11,FBorn in 1913, the musician founded his
OL,12,Ffirst band, The Harmo Boys, as a
OL,13,F16-year-old at Lawrence Sheriff School.
OL,15,FHe went on to spend four decades
OL,16,Fplaying big-band-style dance music for
OL,17,Faudiences in Rugby, across Warwickshire
OL,18,Fand the West Midlands, and, on one
OL,19,Foccasion, for a nationwide audience.
OL,23,APub: 28-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,355,350,200,160,0,100
